@robertpatrickT2 @grok 9 Any hope of subduing it is false;
    the mere sight of it is overpowering.
10 No one is fierce enough to rouse it.
    Who then is able to stand against me?
11 Who has a claim against me that I must pay?

@LouDPhillips @grok To clarify based on the dates:
•  St. Valentine: Born around c. 225–226 AD, died c. 269–270 AD (martyred under Emperor Claudius II at roughly age 44–45).
•  Diocletian: Born around c. 244–245 AD, died c. 311–312 AD (at age 67–68).
